{"name":"English Holly","hex":"#274234","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"english","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Spinning or rotary motion given to a ball around the vertical axis, as in pool, billiards or bowling; spin, sidespin.","An unusual or unexpected interpretation of a text or idea, a spin, a nuance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative form of English."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/english"},{"term":"holly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various shrubs or (mostly) small trees, of the genus Ilex, either evergreen or deciduous, used as decoration especially at Christmas.","The wood from this tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holly"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ilex aquifolium","blocks":[{"text":"Ilex aquifolium, the holly, common holly, English holly, European holly, or occasionally Christmas holly, is a species of flowering plant in the family Aquifoliaceae, native to western and southern Europe, northwest Africa, and southwest Asia. It is regarded as the type species of the genus Ilex, which by association is also called holly. It is an evergreen tree or shrub found, for example, in shady areas of forests of oak and in beech hedges. In the British Isles it is one of very few native hardwood evergreen trees. It has a great capacity to adapt to different conditions and is a pioneer species that repopulates the margins of forests or clearcuts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Ilex-aquifolium_%28Europaeische_Stechpalme-1%29.jpg/330px-Ilex-aquifolium_%28Europaeische_Stechpalme-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ilex_aquifolium"},{"title":"Holly","blocks":[{"text":"Ilex or holly is a genus of over 570 species of flowering plants in the family Aquifoliaceae, and the only living genus in that family. Ilex has the most species of any woody dioecious angiosperm genus. The species are evergreen or deciduous trees, shrubs, and climbers from tropics to temperate zones worldwide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Ilex-aquifolium_%28Europaeische_Stechpalme-1%29.jpg/330px-Ilex-aquifolium_%28Europaeische_Stechpalme-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holly"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Ilex_aquifolium_in_the_Tashkent_Botanical_Garden.jpg/500px-Ilex_aquifolium_in_the_Tashkent_Botanical_Garden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Ilex_aquifolium_in_the_Tashkent_Botanical_Garden.jpg/1280px-Ilex_aquifolium_in_the_Tashkent_Botanical_Garden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Ilex_aquifolium_in_the_Tashkent_Botanical_Garden.jpg/500px-Ilex_aquifolium_in_the_Tashkent_Botanical_Garden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ilex aquifolium","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIlex_aquifolium_in_the_Tashkent_Botanical_Garden.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Ilex_aquifolium_berries_rime.jpg/500px-Ilex_aquifolium_berries_rime.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Ilex_aquifolium_berries_rime.jpg/1280px-Ilex_aquifolium_berries_rime.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Ilex_aquifolium_berries_rime.jpg/500px-Ilex_aquifolium_berries_rime.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Frosted foliage and berries","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w